BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-189486@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260625T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260625T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260625T183000
SUMMARY:Meet the Maker: Rhonda Kallman from Boston Harbor Distillery
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: unli
 mited\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/189486\n\nJoin u
 s for a spirited evening celebrating 250 years of Massachusetts in partner
 ship with Boston Harbor Distillery. Led by founder Rhonda Kallman\, this r
 eception-style Meet the Maker invites members to explore the stories\, cra
 ftsmanship\, and local history woven into one of Boston’s most distincti
 ve distilleries—where every detail\, from the spirits themselves to the 
 names on the bottles\, reflects a deep connection to place.\n\nA pioneerin
 g force in the craft beverage industry\, Rhonda Kallman has spent decades 
 shaping the future of American brewing and distilling. Her passion for whi
 skey\, storytelling\, and craftsmanship is at the heart of Boston Harbor D
 istillery’s approach: honoring history while redefining what modern Amer
 ican spirits can be.\n\nGuided by Rhonda\, members will have the first opp
 ortunity to taste an exclusive selections from Boston Harbor Distillery in
 cluding: Putnam Single Malt Whiskey & Rye Expressions\, Demon Seed Whiskey
  and featuring American 250 Custom Malt Whiskey\, of which only one barrel
  was produced. Set within the legacy of a restored 19th-century waterfront
  mill building in Dorchester\, the distillery has become a modern landmark
  of American craft spirits—equal parts innovation\, heritage\, and unapo
 logetic Boston character.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for
  members only. Complimentary light bites will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/189486
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage
END:VEVENT
