BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-192120@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260626T100000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260626T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260626T113000
SUMMARY:Coffee & Conversation: Inclusion in a Divided World with Lord John 
 Mann 
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: unlimit
 ed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/192120\n\n10:00AM R
 eception\, 10:30AM Discussion \nAs Boston comes together with the global 
 community this summer through events such as the FIFA World Cup and Tall S
 hips\, there is no better time to reflect on collective inclusion and effo
 rts to diminish discrimination.\n\nIn this special edition of Coffee & Con
 versation\, join Lord John Mann\, the United Kingdom Government's Independ
 ent Adviser on Antisemitism\, and Colette Phillips\, President and CEO of 
 Colette Phillips Communications and founder of Get Konnected!\, for a time
 ly discussion on inclusion\, discrimination\, and the challenges facing de
 mocratic societies today.\n\nLord Mann has led groundbreaking initiatives 
 to combat hate in sport\, delivering educational programs to thousands acr
 oss professional football clubs and creating recognized Jewish Supporters 
 Groups that promote inclusion and belonging. Drawing on his experience in 
 government\, sport\, and civil society\, Lord Mann will offer valuable ins
 ights on building stronger and more resilient communities.\n\nTogether\, L
 ord Mann and Colette Phillips will explore how institutions\, communities\
 , and individuals can help build more inclusive societies\, confront preju
 dice\, and foster meaningful dialogue in an increasingly complex world.\n\
 n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Light bites a
 nd refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/192120
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
