BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-191160@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260630T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260630T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260630T183000
SUMMARY:Rethinking Women's Health: Mental Health & Modern Life
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: Health & Wellness\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: un
 limited\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/191160\n\n5:00
 PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion \nMental health is finally getting the a
 ttention it deserves—but the conversation is only beginning.\n\nJoin us 
 for the fourth installment of Rethinking Women's Health\, our ongoing seri
 es exploring the evolving landscape of women's well-being through the lens
  of today's leading physicians\, researchers\, and advocates. This session
  turns its focus to mental health\, examining the intersection of mind\, b
 ody\, identity\, and culture while challenging outdated approaches to care
 .\n\nEach speaker will bring one topic to the conversation\, offering a di
 stinct perspective on women's mental health today. Topics will include tra
 uma-informed care and ketamine-assisted psychotherapy\, the realities of n
 avigating modern womanhood in a rapidly changing cultural landscape\, and 
 the structural and psychological factors that make mental wellness both de
 eply personal and profoundly complex.\n\nLeading the discussion are Dr. Ce
 cil R. Webster Jr.\, Harvard-trained psychiatrist\, psychoanalyst\, and fo
 under of Webster Clinic\; Dr. Marni Chanoff\, Harvard-trained psychiatrist
 \, educator\, and founder of Joy In Health\; and Dr. Jackie Buchanan\, Ha
 rvard-trained child\, adolescent\, and adult psychiatrist.\n\nDesigned to
  offer practical tools\, fresh perspectives\, and meaningful insights\, th
 e evening will conclude with 30 minutes of audience discussion and Q&A. We
  encourage attendees to bring their own questions and curiosities as we cr
 eate a thoughtful space for open and engaging conversation.\n\n*This event
  is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites
  will be served\, and beverages will be available for purchase.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/191160
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness
END:VEVENT
